  "scope": "Constructs a deterministic removed-noise covariance matrix C_S from actual original Wilson block conditional expectations. It is symmetric PSD; full covariance minus C_S equals the true retained covariance. Independent blocks give a finite stencil with at most 24 neighbors, |C_S(p,q)|<=16 and row absolute sum<=384. Actual floor/residue no-wrap geometry makes the sampled a^-8 kernel vanish outside distance 4a on each fixed compact region once the physical period is large. A hard near-diagonal tube has proved absolute mass at most M_R/a^4, M_R=2048*pi^2*volume(closedBall(0,R)). A fourth-order diagonal Taylor counterterm computed from that actual kernel leaves an O(a) remainder on compact two-point tests, uniformly in coupling and period under the stated no-wrap condition; the counterterm vanishes away from the diagonal. Exact finite-cell Fubini binds the physical tensor pairing to actual rescaled original-minus-retained covariance, yielding the repaired-covariance O(a) reduction. Separately constructs every ordered mixed derivative of finite-dimensional source generating functions with deterministic symmetric quadratic matrices, binds the actual C_S correction to the Wilson measure, and identifies corrected second derivatives with retained covariance. Higher corrected jets are not identified with retained moments. Quadratic factors alter only the second connected derivative at zero source, and leave every order>=3 connected derivative unchanged at any source. Every fixed natural moment of the actual microscopic one-link excess converges to the Gamma(3/2) rising-product moment uniformly in varying volumes; its third/fourth cumulant polynomials tend to 3 and 9. These are local noise moments, not physical continuum correlations. Retained estimates, repeated interacting integration, full Schwartz tails, generating reflection covariance and the continuum theory remain open.",
  "actual_two_point_repair": {
    "matrix": "C_S(p,q)=E_original[(F_p-E[F_p|outside S])(F_q-E[F_q|outside S])]. It is deterministic, symmetric and PSD. Cov_full-C_S=Cov_retained.",
    "locality": "For an independent block, C_S(p,q)=0 unless a selected link touches both source plaquettes; at most 24 neighbors and row absolute sum<=384. Literal floor/ZMod sampling gives physical range 4a on fixed radius-R supports when 2R+2a<n*a.",
    "mass": "The hard tube ||x||<=R,||y-x||<=4a has exact four-dimensional displacement volume 128*pi^2*a^4. |C|<=16 and scaling a^-8 give massConstant R/a^4, with massConstant R=2048*pi^2*volume(closedBall(0,R)).",
    "contact": "contact4 integrates the degree 4 relative-coordinate Taylor jet based at (x,x) against the actual tube-truncated kernel. Its coefficients may depend on position and cutoff, and its base-support cutoff R is explicit.",
    "bound": "|pairing(K_a,F)-contact4_a(F)| <= (massConstant R*4^5/24)*seminorm(0,5)(F)*a on fixed compact supports, with proved no-wrap geometry. No coupling or covariance-bound premise is supplied.",
    "tensor_binding": "For real physical Schwartz f,g, the literal sampled kernel integral equals a^-8 times actual original-minus-retained source covariance. Exact finite-cell sums and Fubini retain all periodic aliases and have no extra cell-volume factor.",
    "reduction": "a^-8 Cov_full - contact4(f tensor g) = a^-8 Cov_retained + O(a) on fixed compact real tensor smears.",
    "scope": "This controls one removed covariance. The retained term is not bounded here; subtracting the sum of original-law color matrices is not a proved successive integration. Full Schwartz tails and canonical global contact compatibility remain separate."
  },
  "finite_source_construction": {
    "generating": "exp(-1/2 t^T C_S t) E_original exp(sum_i t_i(F_i-EF_i)), for any finite family of actual plaquette sources.",
    "derivatives": "An explicit multivariable polynomial recurrence constructs every ordered mixed derivative under the original compact measure, with differentiation justified by compact domination.",
    "second_order": "Corrected mixed second derivatives equal actual retained-law covariance; separated second forms agree under the proved no-shared-link condition.",
    "higher_orders": "No equality of higher corrected jets with retained moments is asserted. Quadratic deterministic factors leave connected derivatives of all orders>=3 unchanged.",
    "reflection": "The actual block matrix has no newly proved full generating reflection-positivity theorem. Reflection covariance of the chosen block or a symmetrized construction remains necessary. Existing local contact-factor identities are separately bound to finite source matrices.",
    "hierarchy": "Finite-source jets are not a common continuous full-Schwartz hierarchy with cutoff-independent bounds."
  },
  "local_all_moments": {
    "observable": "X=2 beta(||A||-<q,A>) under the original Wilson law and its actual conditional exterior; this is the previously defined microscopic excess, not the a^-4 smeared plaquette field.",
    "limit": "For each natural m, E X^m -> product_{j=0}^{m-1}(3/2+j), uniformly over arbitrary varying periods>1 as beta->infinity.",
    "bounds": "An explicit order-dependent finite momentBound controls all nonnegative conditional tilts. The original-law error combines O(1/(beta*r0)) with the proved bad-staple probability; no concentration premise is supplied.",
    "nonGaussian": "Third centered moment->3 and fourth cumulant polynomial->9. These identify non-Gaussian microscopic noise only, and do not prove divergent higher smeared connected correlations."
  },
